# rsync --exclude patterns for bin/sync-dotfiles and bin/sync-dotfiles-prune.
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# Pattern syntax matches rsync's --exclude (glob-style, not full gitignore).
#
# Whenever you add a new tracked app (e.g., a new editor or terminal),
# add its cache/state subdirs here so they don't end up in the repo.

# === Editor / OS metadata ===
*.swp
*.swo
*.bak
*~
.DS_Store
.Trash-*

# === Locks / IPC (created by Chrome, Firefox, Electron apps, etc.) ===
*.lock
*.lck
LOCK
LOCKFILE
SingletonLock
.parentlock
Socket
.sock
.lockfile

# === Per-machine / per-user overrides ===
*.local
machine-id

# === Generic cache directories (case-sensitive, common patterns) ===
Cache
cache
"Code Cache"
"Cache Storage"
CachedData
CachedExtensions
CodeCache
GPUCache
WasmTtsEngine
ShaderCache
GrShaderCache
dawn_cache
DawnCache
DawnGraphiteCache
DawnWebGPUCache
GraphiteDawnCache
comptime.dat
.v8_cache

# === Web storage and databases ===
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
IndexedDB
"Local Storage"
"Session Storage"
"Service Worker"
"File System"
databases
blob_storage
Storage

# === Chromium / Chrome / Brave / Edge / Vivaldi / Opera / Ferdium / Discord / Slack / VSCode / Cursor / 1Password / Signal / Spotify / Steam ===
